> Hello,
>
> I'm trying to test using simmer.mon's monitor_dbi function but am running into some trouble... I had to make my own verrsion of the monitor_dbi function becuase the NetezzaSQL database I am trying to write to doesn't support BIT as a column type.

But how do you make the connection to the database? In principle, you
need a DBI-compliant interface, which should work out that issue
automagically, and everything should just be fine. The only
DBI-compliant interface for Netezza I managed to find is this one:
https://github.com/philippechataignon/RNetezza.

